179:We estimated a normative model of gray matter voxelwise asymmetry based on a large neurotypical cohort and applied this to a large, deeply phenotyped, and heterogeneous autism sample. Our results con /uniFB01 rm that atypical asymmetry is a core feature of the autism neurophenotype, shows highly individualized patterns across individuals and is differentially related to different symptom pro /uniFB01 les, such as LD. Further exploration of such associations has the potential to yield clinically relevant strati /uniFB01 cation markers needed for precision medicine.
